stion/problem "Find the slope of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=-7\\operatorname{arccsc} x$ at $x=\\sqrt{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccsc} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7\\operatorname{arccsc} x) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{5}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}) & =\\frac{7}{|\\sqrt{5}|\\sqrt{{\\sqrt{5}}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{5-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "003b3e3a-219a-5a63-82f9-e114c9b4d37e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244302} {:answer/id #uuid "7bfce65e-8edd-5eb9-8109-7bfded382ddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245400} {:answer/id #uuid "cb129f6f-8bae-5b10-9445-3a48d828ffb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246123} {:answer/id #uuid "e424bc2c-c9b0-54ec-ac45-cdf316570410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x}}+\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246342} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d60c5c-939e-553d-8a88-0311bdb31b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d60c5c-939e-553d-8a88-0311bdb31b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246447} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0f6b5ea-57a6-5c54-8af0-7276b65f1d99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df356eaf-6e61-57d5-a6b9-0f0386234268" :question/math-academy-id "q-110517" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}+5\\operatorname{arccsc} x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccsc} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{x}+5\\operatorname{arccsc} x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+5\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdcb8335-d77f-5744-a62d-d1e124d9d3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296345} {:answer/id #uuid "7f99e84a-7088-47c4-b31b-db2302410090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}+\\frac{2x}{x^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186748190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdcb8335-d77f-5744-a62d-d1e124d9d3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296345} :answer-field/id #uuid "d21e2329-6733-5a78-a5e9-3327d19b15b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297073}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "75fdefb6-9025-5f7e-8537-d9b67757e76d" :question/math-academy-id "q-312358" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\operatorname{arccot} x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1),$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8ee806f-7719-5298-ac62-41e17b9b6edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8ee806f-7719-5298-ac62-41e17b9b6edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313414} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3d1446c-0422-5804-ab35-51c287ebd71b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314497}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d8da40e-cfdf-5c60-a36a-cdb26f7bb8fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-341104" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x+\\operatorname{arccot} x$ at $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+\\operatorname{arccot} x) \\\\  & =2+\\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={y}^{′}(0) & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "574af7f2-928a-5a00-b135-4916a6dec950" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339926} {:answer/id #uuid "987816d8-ddea-5472-bfa6-60df165674be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340500} {:answer/id #uuid "a07504e1-78da-53c1-a071-bf6d07bb482a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340581} {:answer/id #uuid "c71ac88f-b329-53fd-a776-c30ee71c20b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340893} {:answer/id #uuid "c94af7b5-9c00-52e6-891e-6dbf2ca55530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c94af7b5-9c00-52e6-891e-6dbf2ca55530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340913} :answer-field/id #uuid "47d65433-3d6d-5565-a566-451d9ef6b0e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341504}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "077baa93-9f9f-5780-986d-77a93ca959f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-73437" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}-2\\operatorname{arccsc} x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccsc} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}-2\\operatorname{arccsc} x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-2\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746626 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37951037-0063-5fd9-990e-431b896a9d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37951037-0063-5fd9-990e-431b896a9d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746628} :answer-field/id #uuid "a20b0319-8a31-5a92-bbd5-d6df6576f2f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746637}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1abca24a-bd18-5df4-80b7-52b463869515" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x-3\\operatorname{arcsec}x$ at $x=-\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The inverse secant derivative is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec}x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(x)&=2-3\\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\\\\\n&=2-\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the specified input, $|-\\sqrt{3}|=\\sqrt{3}$ and $(-\\sqrt{3})^2-1=2$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=y'(-\\sqrt{3})&=2-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{2}}\\\\\n&=2-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{6}}\\\\\n&=2-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value keeps the denominator positive even though the input is negative. Since $-\\sqrt{3}<-1$, the derivative exists here."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746635 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be1f69d-7af9-5f08-a3ff-db4a9c4809b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746627} {:answer/id #uuid "510e34c2-a1f1-500f-9dc5-4d807479ca7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746630} {:answer/id #uuid "60d62bd2-4f43-5d3b-8b2f-3188decb0c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746631} {:answer/id #uuid "765ee9ed-8b00-53ed-9a30-d02fe3a8ec88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746633} {:answer/id #uuid "7c18e5ca-82d5-5954-9c66-1eff316c9ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "510e34c2-a1f1-500f-9dc5-4d807479ca7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746630} :answer-field/id #uuid "75261e29-1775-5f6b-b578-0c5ff188ed86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746632}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ca226a1-3aaa-542c-bc08-eb209e0b2aa2" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}-3\\operatorname{arccsc}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The inverse cosecant derivative is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc}x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum, constant multiple, and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=2\\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\right)-3\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe negative coefficient and the negative inverse cosecant derivative give a positive second term. This derivative is valid for $x>1$, the interior of the function's real domain."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746638 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e3b694b-eb90-5928-a554-bfa0ff16ce82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e3b694b-eb90-5928-a554-bfa0ff16ce82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746636} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ce6588a-82c1-5fd7-98c8-cd37fa2e032b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746629}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fad14dae-b314-5780-86a8-6f9980b62e4e" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x-3\\operatorname{arccot}x$ at $x=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The inverse cotangent derivative is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot}x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate using the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'(x)&=2-3\\left(-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\right)\\\\\n&=2+\\frac{3}{1+x^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe tangent slope is the derivative at the specified input:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm=y'(1)&=2+\\frac{3}{1+1^2}\\\\\n&=2+\\frac{3}{2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{7}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dae4796-963e-5908-816a-f473ba9af8da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x + 1}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dae4796-963e-5908-816a-f473ba9af8da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x + 1}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746722} :answer-field/id #uuid "e29eec5c-822f-54e6-9bb8-4182ec89796c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746729}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22eb5c53-75fa-548b-a7eb-d4c6161f4550" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=-\\operatorname{arccot}x+2\\ln(1+x^2).$\n\n$f'(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the derivative of the inverse function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot}x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules, and differentiate the logarithm:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+x^2}+\\frac{4x}{1+x^2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{4 x + 1}{1+x^2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis derivative is valid for $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef049f16-614b-5703-a1f8-7bee429d1925" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x + 1}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef049f16-614b-5703-a1f8-7bee429d1925" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x + 1}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746730} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7b5bee8-8b53-54e6-a5dc-577498d1fb54" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746728}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3378f3b1-4568-5a7c-bc3a-b01c6bac7b41" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=-\\operatorname{arccot}x+\\ln(1+x^2).$\n\n$f'(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the derivative of the inverse function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot}x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules, and differentiate the logarithm:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+x^2}+\\frac{2x}{1+x^2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 x + 1}{1+x^2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis derivative is valid for $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12eabe91-d2a4-5524-ab1f-e0a17fd4d710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x + 2}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12eabe91-d2a4-5524-ab1f-e0a17fd4d710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x + 2}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746716} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab91eec3-9437-5e4f-8f02-e0d902a8cfb3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746724}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6c5cca2-3c4d-522e-8270-f5f5d1f3cc60" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{arccot}x+\\ln(1+x^2).$\n\n$f'(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the derivative of the inverse function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot}x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules, and differentiate the logarithm:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{2}{1+x^2}+\\frac{2x}{1+x^2}\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 x + 2}{1+x^2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis derivative is valid for $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746726 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2dde8f4-d609-5531-b534-8169d80b204b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2dde8f4-d609-5531-b534-8169d80b204b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746723} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d83fc59-8a38-5a07-ab9f-01238b4c3704" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746721}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc3428d3-d5d1-53a7-965d-769a32e5034a" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}+5\\operatorname{arccsc}x.$\n\n$f'(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the derivative of the inverse function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc}x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules, with the power rule for the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=2\\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\right)+5\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis derivative is valid for $x>1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c1a992b-ba55-5b92-88d3-bfa992c97421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c1a992b-ba55-5b92-88d3-bfa992c97421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746717} :answer-field/id #uuid "38550d25-3b90-5220-94a0-5e15b32c89ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746720}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2c8f3d5-5d08-5fa0-bda2-699365af3066" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+3\\operatorname{arcsec}x.$\n\n$f'(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the derivative of the inverse function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec}x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nApply the sum and constant multiple rules, with the power rule for the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=1\\left(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\right)+3\\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis derivative is valid for $x>1$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}]}
